From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Type Application-Server-ID as UTF8String

3GPP TS 32.299 table 7.2.0.1 types AVP 2101 only "refer [223]",
OMA-DDS-Charging_Data, the document that defines it. Its approved V1.0
(OMA-DDS-Charging_Data-V1_0-20110201-A), table 11 in clause 8.4, types
Application-Server-Id (vendor 10415, code 2101) UTF8String; clause 6.2.5
describes it as identifying "the application server providing the
service". As Unsigned32, any identifier but a four-octet one is
reported malformed.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..7950288 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -6943,7 +6943,7 @@
 			<type type-name="OctetString"/>
 		</avp>
 		<avp name="Application-Server-ID" code="2101" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
-			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+			<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
 		</avp>
 		<avp name="Application-Service-Type" code="2102" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
 			<type type-name="Enumerated"/>
